== Railways ==
{{main|Rail transport in Angola}}
There are three separate railway lines in Angola:
* [[Luanda Railway]] ([[Caminhos de Ferro de Luanda|CFL]]) (northern);
* [[Benguela Railway]] ([[Caminho de Ferro de Benguela|CFB]]) (central), operated by the [[Lobito Atlantic Railway]] joint venture;
* [[Moçâmedes Railway]] ([[Moçâmedes Railway|CFM]]) (southern);

Reconstruction of these three lines began in 2005 and they are now all operational. The [[Benguela Railway]] connects to the [[Democratic Republic of the Congo]].

